# dependencies
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js

# builds
.next/
out/
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# env — never commit secrets
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# logs & runtime
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.pids
*.pid

# NOTE: apps/agent/logs/decisions.jsonl is intentionally NOT ignored.
# The hash-chained decision log is part of the research record and must be
# committed — it is a submission checklist item (build spec §17).

# NOTE: apps/agent/logs/decisions-llm.jsonl is intentionally NOT ignored either.
# There are two committed records because there are two kinds of session, and
# `generator` on every entry says which one produced it — decisions.jsonl is the
# deterministic session, decisions-llm.jsonl is the one a model proposed. Keeping
# them in one file would mean one of the two facts got overwritten, and the whole
# point of the field is that neither fact is hidden.

# Scratch output from a reproduction check — the `out` the demo-run workflow
# tells you to pass when you want to re-run a session without writing either
# committed document. A record of a check is not a record of the project.
decisions-check.jsonl

# NOTE: apps/agent/data/frozen/ is intentionally NOT ignored.
# The frozen partition datasets are the artifact the whole provenance claim
# rests on: every verdict's dataset_sha256 refers to these exact bytes, so a
# reader must be able to fetch them and recompute the hash. ~3.5 MB total.
# Verify before committing with:
#   node --experimental-strip-types apps/agent/scripts/rebuild-manifest.ts --check

# local verification scratch — regenerated by apps/agent/_regen-scratch.sh.
# Production compiles src/*.ts -> dist/*.js with tsc; _scratch exists only so
# the TypeScript can be run directly through Node's type stripping on a machine
# that cannot run a full install. Never committed.
_scratch/
_dbg*.mjs
_e2e.mjs
# Hand-written stand-ins for the two packages src/index.ts imports (express,
# cors), kept OUTSIDE _scratch so a regen cannot delete them. _regen-scratch.sh
# copies them back in. Never committed — they are not the real packages and must
# never be mistaken for them.
_stubs/
# Verification probes — the controls that check the harness can detect what it
# claims to detect. Kept OUTSIDE _scratch for the same reason as _stubs:
# _regen-scratch.sh does `rm -rf _scratch`, and a probe that has to be rewritten
# after every regen is a probe that stops being run. The script copies them back
# in. Never committed — they are local verification, not the project's tests.
_probes/

# os / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# python (recon scripts)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Working briefs handed to me, not project artefacts. The repo is what judges
# read; these are notes about how to build it, and they name files that do not
# exist and changes that were already made. Ignored rather than left untracked
# so a `git add .` cannot publish them by accident.
factor_prover_ui_redesign_brief.md
factor_prover_ui_fix_exact.md
# The v2 reconfiguration brief is the same class of file as the two above, and it
# was left merely untracked until 2026-09-24 — at which point a `git add -A` did
# try to publish its 3111 lines. The comment above describes exactly that
# accident; this line is what makes the comment true.
FACTOR_PROVER_UI_UX_RECONFIGURATION_v2.md

# Submission notes are local-only: they carry strategy, gap analysis and the
# pre-submission checklist. Not for the public repo.
SUBMISSION.md

# Local-only working documents: submission text, recording guide, the LLM
# answer. These carry strategy and are kept off the public repo.
DEMO_RECORDING_GUIDE.md
LLM_ROLE.md
PROJECT_DESCRIPTION.md
TRACK_DECISION.md
TURN_ON_LIVE_EXECUTION.md

# Handover notes on the Bitget GetAgent / Agent Hub / paper-trading side,
# written 2026-09-24 for a second model to read. Same class as SUBMISSION.md:
# it is a briefing about the project, not an artefact of it. It also quotes the
# demo order ids and the exact refusal text, and restates the gap analysis —
# none of which belongs in front of a judge as project documentation.
HANDOVER_GETAGENT.md

# Review brief written 2026-09-25 for a second model to check the evidence-record
# work rather than take it on trust. Same class as the two above: it is an account
# OF the project rather than an artefact of it, it names the exact gaps in the
# verification, and it restates the standing instructions on what must not be
# published. Ignored rather than untracked, for the reason recorded in the commit
# that added HANDOVER_GETAGENT.md: untracked is one `git add -A` from published.
REVIEW_BRIEF.md

# demo-local/ — the demo video's script and recording recipe.
#
# Both were previously published: the script lived at docs/DEMO_SCRIPT.md and
# was tracked from the day it was written, and the guide sat at the repo root.
# They are strategy documents — they tell the presenter what to say and which
# detail to cut under time pressure — so they belong with the other submission
# material rather than in the public repository. The whole directory is ignored
# rather than the two files, so anything else that lands in here stays local by
# default instead of by remembering.
#
# NOTE: ignoring this now does not unpublish the earlier commits. The script's
# older revisions remain in the repository's history and are still readable at
# their commit SHAs; this stops it appearing in the working tree of a fresh
# clone and in the tip of every branch from here on.
demo-local/
